        "syllabus": "### 主要教科書及其他參考書\n(Level B): American English File 2, third edition by Latham-Koenig, Oxenden, and Lambert. OUP (2021).\nISBN 978-0-19-490639-5\n\n### 課程簡介\n本課程乃是針對非英文系之大一學生開設，透過課堂英文教材與活動以及線上自學練習，期望有效提升英文字彙、文法及聽說讀寫能力、培養學生學習英文的習慣與興趣、以及激發持續精進學術及職場英文能力。\n\n為提升學生英語素養，每學期外語教學中心舉辦英語相關競賽，培養學生自主強化口說能力。每班擇優參加外語教學中心舉辦之正式比賽。\n\n我們亦鼓勵學生自行參與線上模擬測驗以檢測學生英語學習成果，增進學生英檢考試的應考能力。預期學生於課程結束時英檢測驗達到等同CEFR B1之程度。\n共同暨通識課程教育目標\n一、健全身心發展，豐富靈性生活。\n二、深化語文應用，涵育國際視野。\n三、激發多元敘事，涵養議題綜整。\n四、提升科技知能，強化創新服務。\n五、理解多元社會，善盡公民責任。\n六、促進利他精神，落實社會實踐。\n\n### 評分方式及比重\n1. Attendance/ Quizzes / Homework etc...: 30%\n2. Midterm Project: 30%\n3. Final Exam: 30%\n4. Participation of activities: 10%\n\n### 學生能力指標與權重\n| 能力指標 | 權重(%) |\n| --- | --- |\n| A. 獨立思維與問題解決能力。 | 10 |\n| B. 規律運動的自主能力。 | 0 |\n| C. 閱讀理解與跨域敘事能力。 | 10 |\n| H. 正確流暢的語用能力。 | 50 |\n| J. 生命價值與生態關懷能力。 | 0 |\n| K. 多元文化欣賞與社會參與能力。 | 20 |\n| L. 資訊科技的運用能力。 | 0 |\n| M. 策略發展與團隊協作能力。 | 10 |\n\n### 課程之整體規劃與設計\n| 具體教學目標 | 核心能力 | 教學策略 | 評量方法 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1. Understanding a description. 2. Understanding the key events in a story and checking the hypothesis (using visual evidence). 3. Understanding text cohesion – connectors; a questionnaire, and rules of a game. 4. Understanding opinions and checking and correction information. 5. Scanning for data (facts and numbers) and identifying pros and cons. | A, C, H, K, M | 講述法、小組合作、反覆練習法(例如,英聽)、問答法、學生上台報告 | 小考、期中考、期末考、出席率、上課參與討論、同儕互評 |\n\n### 授課進度與內容\n| 週次 | 主題內容/章節/活動 | 備註 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Course orientation | *NOTE: supplemental to Level 2: Sustainable Development Goals book - (SDG) Classes begin on September 8. |\n| 2 | UNIT 1A: Are you? Can you? Do you? Did you? | SDGs 1-3, 11-13 |\n| 3 | UNIT 1B: The perfect date? | SDGs 4-6, 14-16 |\n| 4 | UNIT 1C: The Remake Project | SDGs 10-13 Sept. 28 (Sunday) – Confucius’ Birthday (Teacher’s Day) and Teacher Appreciation Day September 29 (Monday) – Substitute holiday for Confucius’ Birthday (Teacher’s Day) and Teacher Appreciation Day, as it falls on a regular holiday. |\n| 5 | UNIT 1C: The Remake Project OR UNIT 2A: OMG! Where’s my passport? | SDGs 7-9 Oct. 6 (Mon.) Mid-Autumn Festival -Day off Oct. 10 (Fri.) Double Tenth Day- Day off |\n| 6 | UNIT 1C: The Remake Project OR UNIT 2A: OMG! Where’s my passport? OR UNIT 2B: That’s me in the picture! | SDGs 2-5, 17 |\n| 7 | UNIT 2A: OMG! Where’s my passport? OR UNIT 2B: That’s me in the picture! OR UNIT 2C: One dark October evening | SDGs 8-11, 15 October 24 (Friday)– substitute holiday for Taiwan Retrocession Day and the Anniversary of the Battle of Guningtou, as it falls on a regular holiday. October 25 (Saturday) – Taiwan Retrocession Day and the Anniversary of the Battle of Guningtou |\n| 8 | Midterm Project |  |\n| 9 | UNIT 2B: That’s me in the picture! OR UNIT 2C: One dark October evening OR UNIT 3A: TripAside | SDGs 12-16 |\n| 10 | UNIT 2C: One dark October evening OR UNIT 3A: TripAside OR UNIT 3B: Put it on your calendar! | SDGs 5-7, 9 |\n| 11 | UNIT 3A: TripAside OR UNIT 3B: Put it on your calendar! OR UNIT 3C: Word games | SDGs 6-10, 11 |\n| 12 | UNIT 3B: Put it on your calendar! OR UNIT 3C: Word games | SDGs 11, 13, 15 Nov. 26 (Wed.) Sports Day-No classes |\n| 13 | UNIT 3C: Word games Review | SDGs 2, 6, 14 |\n| 14 | Review. Thursday class: Final Exam UNIT 4A: Who does what? | Dec. 11 (Thurs.) 15:00-17:00 Freshman English Unified Final Exam in the computer classroom |\n| 15 | Final Exam UNIT 4B: In your cart | SDGs 7, 12, 13 Dec. 18 (Thurs.) 15:00-17:00 Freshman English Unified Final Exam in the computer classroom |\n| 16 | Final Exam. UNIT 4C: #greatweekend | SDGs 8-16 Dec. 25 (Thurs.) Constitution Day, Christmas Day, and University Anniversary Day |\n| 17 | Multiple and creative teaching | Jan. 1 (Thurs.) Founding Day of the Republic of China (Taiwan) -Day off Jan. 2 (Fri.) Flexible day off |\n| 18 | Multiple and creative teaching |  |\n\n\n---"
