        "syllabus": "### 主要教科書及其他參考書\nTextbook:\n動畫圖解資料結構使用C，滄海書局(CS0357)\nAuthor: 李春雄\nLecture Notes in PDF\n\n### 課程簡介\n資料結構是設計電腦程式的基礎知識，欲使程式設計得有效率，非熟悉資料結構不可。資料結構課程包括學習設計程式時常用的各種資料，如堆疊、佇列、堆積、二元樹、圖形等結構及其特性。另外亦包含學習設計演算法以有效的使用此資料結構。\n1. Array\n2. Stacks\n3. Queues\n3. Linked list\n4. Trees\n5. Graphs\n\n### 評分方式及比重\nThe grading policy states as follows:\n基本上根據院定必修評分標準\n1. Class achievements (小考或課堂成績）: 30%\n2. Min-term examination: 35%\n3. Final examination: 35%\n4. Programming exercise: 5%\n\n\nATTENTION:\n1. 考試不可作弊, 作業不可抄襲. 違者依校規處理.\n2. 小考,期中考或期末考累計缺考三次(含)以上, 學期成績可以零分計算\n\n### 學生能力指標與權重\n| 能力指標 | 權重(%) |\n| --- | --- |\n| A. 數學、科學及工程的預備知識。 | 40 |\n| B. 資訊領域在各種行業的應用與對環境、社會的影響。 | 0 |\n| C. 現代各種資訊軟、硬體工具的應用能力。 | 0 |\n| D. 程式的設計與分析能力，程式所得數據的詮釋能力。 | 0 |\n| E. 資訊系統的分析與設計能力。 | 40 |\n| F. 專案分析、規劃及執行的能力。 | 10 |\n| G. 書面報告與技術文件的編寫與維護能力。 | 10 |\n| H. 團隊合作及專業倫理的觀念。 | 0 |\n| I. 終身學習的觀念與習慣。 | 0 |\n\n### 課程之整體規劃與設計\n| 具體教學目標 | 核心能力 | 教學策略 | 評量方法 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 能分析不同演算法的複雜度 | A, E, F, G | 講述法、個案討論 | 小考、期中考、期末考 |\n| 能撰寫程式實作各類資料結構 | A, E, F, G | 講述法、上機/實務操作 | 小考、期中考、期末考、實驗操作 |\n| 能熟悉各種資料結構的特性及用途 | A, E, F, G | 講述法、上機/實務操作 | 小考、期中考、期末考、上課參與討論 |\n| 具備利用各類資料結構解決問題的能力 | A, E, F, G | 講述法、個案討論、上機/實務操作 | 小考、期中考、期末考、上課參與討論、實驗操作 |\n\n### 授課進度與內容\n| 週次 | 主題內容/章節/活動 | 備註 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Introduction to data structures | 1. defining algorithms 2. defining data structures 3. relations between algorithms and data stryuctures 4. Object oriented languages and data structures |\n| 2 | Efficiency of algorithms | 1. Recursive definitions and methods 2. Execution of recursive methods 3. Using recursive methodlogy to solve problems 4. Performance evaluation of Recursive methods |\n| 3 | Linear lists (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. The specification of the list ADT 2. The requirements of the operations applied on lists 3. Implementing lists by using arrays 4. Characteristics of arrays 5. ArrayList class and Vector class in J2SDK 6. Performance evaluation of using array presentation |\n| 4 | Linear lists (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. The specification of the list ADT 2. The requirements of the operations applied on lists 3. Implementing lists by using arrays 4. Characteristics of arrays 5. ArrayList class and Vector class in J2SDK 6. Performance evaluation of using array presentation |\n| 5 | Stacks (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Specification of stacks 2. Details of implementing stacks by arrays 3. Details of implementing stacks by linked lists 4. Expression evaluation |\n| 6 | Stacks (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Specification of stacks 2. Details of implementing stacks by arrays 3. Details of implementing stacks by linked lists 4. Expression evaluation |\n| 7 | Exercise before midterm exam | Exercise before midterm exam |\n| 8 | Midterm exam |  |\n| 9 | Queues (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Specification of queues 2. Details of implementing queues by arrays 3. Details of implementing queues by linked lists 4. Variants of queues |\n| 10 | Queues (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Specification of queues 2. Details of implementing queues by arrays 3. Details of implementing queues by linked lists 4. Variants of queues |\n| 11 | Binary and other trees (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Definition of binary trees 2. Properties of binary trees 3. Terminology of binary trees 4. binary tree traversals 5. Implementing binary trees 6. Huffman coding scheme |\n| 12 | Binary and other trees (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Definition of general trees 2. General trees and binary trees 3. Implementing general trees |\n| 13 | Priority queues (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Definiftion of priority queues 2. Implementation of priority queues by heaps and leftist trees |\n| 14 | Binary search trees and balanced serch trees (along with the assistant of Generative AI) | 1. Definition and usage of comparison trees 2. Efficiency analysis based on comparison trees 3. Operations on binary search trees |\n| 15 | Exercise before the final exam. | Exercise before the final exam. |\n| 16 | Final Exam. | 1. Definition of graphs 2. Terminology related to graphs 3. Implementation of graphs 4. Graph traversals |\n| 17 | Innovative Teaching with the assistant of Generative AI | 1. Definition of graphs 2. Terminology related to graphs 3. Implementation of graphs 4. Graph traversals |\n| 18 | Innovative Teaching with the assistant of Generative AI | 1. Sequential Search 2. Binary Search |\n\n\n---"
